cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "qablate: classical-quantum ablation studies for Bayesian parameter inference"
abstract: >-
  A Python library that swaps the components of Bayesian inference algorithms
  (Metropolis-Hastings proposal and acceptance, variational distribution and
  optimizer, genetic operators) between classical and quantum-circuit
  implementations, one at a time, and checks what changes. It includes flat
  background cosmology models (LambdaCDM, wCDM, CPL, PEDE, GEDE) with H(z) and
  Pantheon 2018 likelihoods. The aim is fidelity to classical results; no
  quantum advantage is claimed.
type: software
